------- FILE main.asm
------- FILE voices.asm LEVEL 2 PASS 3
      0  15ff					      include	"voices.asm"
      1  15ff							; Fat Chip 64 - voice pool and smart stacking (poly synth mode)
      2  15ff							;
      3  15ff							; Nine voices across three chips, interleaved so a stack mixes chips:
      4  15ff							;   v0 SID 1	v1 GB pulse 1	v2 NES pulse 1
      5  15ff							;   v3 SID 2	v4 GB pulse 2	v5 NES pulse 2
      6  15ff							;   v6 SID 3	v7 GB wave*	v8 NES triangle*      (* bass voices)
      7  15ff							; Allocation, whenever the held notes change. Who comes first (v0.21):
      8  15ff							; Polyphony > Fat Bass > the patch's effects (REPEAT's echoes) > stacking.
      9  15ff							;   1. every note gets a voice (SPARKLE's arp pair is what you play, so it
     10  15ff							;	counts as notes and goes first)
     11  15ff							;   2. Fat Bass: as many bass voices as are spare play the lowest note,
     12  15ff							;	folded into the bass range (one note fewer needs a voice, so with
     13  15ff							;	Fat Bass the bottom of the chord is the bass)
     14  15ff							;   3. REPEAT's echo voices: one or two of what's still spare
     15  15ff							;   4. leftover voices stack on the lowest two notes, alternating
     16  15ff							; So one note = a nine-voice unison across three chips, and in chords the
     17  15ff							; bottom of the chord is fattest. Disabled devices, and voices the drums
     18  15ff							; hold (vDrum), get no notes.
     19  15ff
     20  15ff							; ------------------------------------------------------------ SID
     21  15ff				   SidInit
     22  15ff					      subroutine
     23  15ff		       a2 18		      ldx	#24
     24  1601		       a9 00		      lda	#0
     25  1603				   .clr
     26  1603		       9d 00 d4 	      sta	SID,x
     27  1606		       ca		      dex
     28  1607		       10 fa		      bpl	.clr
     29  1609		       20 2c 16 	      jsr	SidVolume
     30  160c		       a2 02		      ldx	#2
     31  160e				   .v
